# Copy to .env and fill in. Only .env is read; keys in your shell are ignored.
# Every key is optional, as long as something can hear, think and speak: TARS uses the services there are keys for and
# says at startup what it does without the others (voice-assistant --check shows it too).
# OpenAI: answers what needs the web, the thinking model, and backs up speech to text; hears and speaks without
# Deepgram, and answers everything without Groq or Cerebras. platform.openai.com
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Deepgram: [stt] provider = "deepgram" or "flux" (OpenAI's otherwise); also the voice, with [tts] provider =
# "deepgram" or without a Cartesia key. console.deepgram.com
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# Cartesia: the voice, [tts] provider = "cartesia" with a Sonic model and cartesia_voice; Deepgram's or OpenAI's
# otherwise. play.cartesia.ai
CARTESIA_API_KEY=
# Cerebras: [llm] cerebras_model, the quick brain; cloud.cerebras.ai
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# Telegram: a bot's token, for [telegram] (chatting with TARS there). Message @BotFather on Telegram and send /newbot.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Home Assistant: a long-lived access token, for [home] (the devices TARS works). In Home Assistant: your profile,
# Security, Long-lived access tokens. docs/home.md
HOME_ASSISTANT_TOKEN=
# A plugin's keys go here too: examples/my_house's IR blaster takes TUYA_LOCAL_KEY (its README says how to find it).
# Routers: each [[presence.routers]]'s admin password, under the name its secret gives (docs/presence.md), like
# ROUTER_PASSWORD=...
# The doors' MQTT broker: TARS's own password on it, under [presence.mqtt] secret's name, like MQTT_PASSWORD=...
# deploy/install-pi.sh makes one, and TARS's user on deploy/home-assistant's Mosquitto (docs/presence.md).
# AWS: an IAM user's access key, for [backup] (backing up to an S3 bucket). docs/backup.md has the policy it needs.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Seals Home Assistant's setup before it goes in the backup ([home] config_dir): voice-assistant --ha-config-key makes
# it. Keep a copy elsewhere too (a password manager): a new machine needs it to open the setup from the backup.
HA_CONFIG_KEY=
# Spotify: your own app's client id from developer.spotify.com, for a kind = "spotify" device. No secret: the sign-in
# is PKCE, done once with `uv run python -m voice_assistant.spotify login`. docs/home.md#spotify
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
